🧠 Short Interview Answers
❓ What is Terraform?

👉
"Terraform is an Infrastructure as Code tool used to provision and manage infrastructure through declarative configuration files."

❓ What is Terraform state?

👉
"Terraform state tracks the resources Terraform manages and maps configuration to real cloud infrastructure."

❓ Why use remote state?

👉
"Remote state supports team collaboration, central storage, and locking to avoid concurrent modifications."

❓ What is drift?

👉
"Drift happens when infrastructure is changed manually outside Terraform, causing mismatch with Terraform state."

❓ Why use modules?

👉
"Modules improve reusability, maintainability, and cleaner infrastructure design."

❓ Difference between `count` and `for_each`?

👉
"`count` uses numeric indexes and is good for identical resources. `for_each` uses keys and is better when resource identity matters."

